---
import { site } from "../data/site";
---
<section class="about" id="about">
  <figure class="stamp rv"><img src="/assets/img/stamp.webp" alt={`${site.name} as a child`} loading="lazy"></figure>
  <div class="rv">
    <h2><span>I've always been</span> better at building.</h2>
    <p>Some people plan on paper. I build to find out.</p>
    <p>I grew up on HTML in a notepad and switched to JavaScript in grade 9. Then came TypeScript at work, React on a deadline and Go on a dare. Five languages, and I've been told I over-engineer in all of them.</p>
    <p>I've shipped to real users, run an on-call rotation, and once put the release notes inside the app to get people to read them. It worked.</p>
    <p>So building for the web makes sense to me. Most products ship faster than they're understood. I'd like to help build the parts that people actually feel.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="polaroid rv" id="polaroid"><img src="/assets/p/polaroid.webp" alt={`${site.name} at work`} loading="lazy"></figure>
</section>
